tches are separately excluded. This is selective contextual evidence, not an automatic rule for every same-spelling word.","sourceHeadwordId":"Peace","term":"Peace"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Peace","sourceTitle":"Peace"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.1-13","r":"Ps.85.1-13","rawR":"Ps.85.1-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.1-13","value":"Ps.85.1-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 85"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist leads the postexilic community in lament and prayer for full redemption. He ponders God’s past rescue of Israel from exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.1-3","r":"Ps.85.1-3","rawR":"Ps.85.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.1-3","value":"Ps.85.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:1-3"},"), longs for greater evidence of God’s goodness, and leads the community in prayer for full restoration (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.4-7","r":"Ps.85.4-7","rawR":"Ps.85.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.4-7","value":"Ps.85.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:4-7"},"). God responds with a message of peace (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.8-9","r":"Ps.85.8-9","rawR":"Ps.85.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.8-9","value":"Ps.85.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:8-9"},"), and the psalm concludes with a lyrical outburst at the grandeur of God’s salvation (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.10-13","r":"Ps.85.10-13","rawR":"Ps.85.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.10-13","value":"Ps.85.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:10-13"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.85.1-13","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":85,"endVerse":13,"startChapter":85,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.85.1-13","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[85],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"28bb16b642dc69faf3209a5091cbad1051b3d234fc1c4aebf7207abe3aa0cab8","sourceItemName":"Ps.85.1-13","sourceMember"